1
00:00:00,550 --> 00:00:06,913
You know that feeling when your coding
agent finishes a change, and it works, but
you couldn't quite explain it yet?

2
00:00:08,380 --> 00:00:09,822
That's why we made Ownit.

3
00:00:10,106 --> 00:00:15,141
When you push, it asks a few short
questions about what changed, right in
your terminal.

4
00:00:16,180 --> 00:00:18,175
Say you added payment retries.

5
00:00:18,459 --> 00:00:19,112
Why?

6
00:00:19,393 --> 00:00:22,072
So a temporary error doesn't lose the
sale.

7
00:00:22,354 --> 00:00:24,414
Just explain it in your own words.

8
00:00:25,480 --> 00:00:30,027
You get feedback, and a passing debrief
marks those commits as verified.

9
00:00:30,312 --> 00:00:31,241
Busy right now?

10
00:00:31,522 --> 00:00:33,201
You can always come back later.

11
00:00:34,247 --> 00:00:36,162
Keep building with your coding agent.

12
00:00:36,447 --> 00:00:39,455
Give yourself a moment to understand what
you're shipping.

13
00:00:39,736 --> 00:00:40,678
That's Ownit.
